  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: the supplied object 'him' (t027) moves from αὐτόν to δείραντες, and αὐτόν keeps only t030, the object of the verb that governs it.",
    "This aligns the verse with 20:11, 20:12, 20:15 and 20:20, where an expressed pronoun goes to its governing verb and each supplied object goes to the English verb requiring it.",
    "Rule 103's resumptive-pronoun contrast (3JN.1.13) is the competing reading and is named in the αὐτόν unit; it is weaker here because a second Greek verb stands in the clause to license the supplied object."
